{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion","id":1341041,"title":"Affinity Sphere confusion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-12T19:51:21-07:00","id":1341041,"title":"Affinity Sphere confusion","content":"I am a bit confused with the definition of Affinity Sphere definition, on M20 p. 257 is stated:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All mages begin with one <b><i>Affinity Sphere</i></b>: the Sphere that<br /> character understands best. Generally, this Sphere is associated<br /> with a mage\u2019s first experience with magick... The first Sphere dot you place is your<br /> Affinity Sphere.<br /> Your character must have at least one dot in one of her group\u2019s<br /> Affinity Spheres. You can choose any allowed Spheres for your mage,<br /> <b><i>so long as you place at least one dot under your group\u2019s Affinity Sphere as<br /> well</i></b>. </div> </div> </div>My questions are: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Do you have one (by being a mage) or two (one by being a mage and one by being a member of a faction) Affinity Spheres?</li> <li>If you only have one Affinity Sphere, does it mean that you cant have for example a Celestial Chorus member with affinity for Entropy?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Thanks for the help","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-12-2019, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T22:27:56-07:00","id":1341054,"title":"","content":"You have one affinity sphere - and the affinity spheres of each group are listed in the group's description <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> List for the traditions (With their most common affinity sphere first):<br /> <br /> Akashics - <b>Mind</b>, Life<br /> Celestial Chorus - <b>Prime</b>, Forces, Spirit<br /> Ecstatics: <b>Time</b>, Life, Mind<br /> Dreamspeakers: <b>Spirit</b>, Forces, Life, Matter<br /> Euthanatos: <b>Entropy</b>, Life, Spirit<br /> Order of Hermes: Almost always <b>Forces</b>; Life, Matter, Mind and Spirit gets used by some houses instead.<br /> Sons of Ether: <b>Matter</b>, Forces, Prime<br /> Verbena: <b>Life</b>, Forces<br /> Virtual Adepts: <b>Correspondence</b>/Data, Forces<br /> <br /> What the text is saying is, that your Mage can have any spheres on their sheet on character generation, but they need at least one dot in their affinity sphere - and by logic, normally their affinity sphere tends to have the most dots. It's the easiest to learn, for them.<br /> <br /> A Chorister with Entropy as their affinity sphere would be very, very unusual - but depending on their paradigm and just how they tend to use Entropy, it could work. You really just have to find a good argument for your ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-13-2019, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T22:59:47-07:00","id":1341059,"title":"","content":"Though I am still trying to learn M20, I had the same question and my ST explained it as this. You can choose any sphere to place your first dot in and that is your Mages affinity sphere. You may then place your other dots but your mages affinity sphere should be never be lower than the others and one of your dots must go in a sphere that your group has affinity with.<br /> <br /> Was that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T23:07:55-07:00","id":1341061,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty correct, mostly. Placing the first dot in an affinity sphere fulfills all the rules.<br /> The affinity sphere *tends* to be the sphere a character is best at. 'All other spheres need to be equal or lower' is not a hard rule, but it is a thing that just makes very much sense - and the lesser XP cost for it during gameplay helps with that, too. Though frankly during actual gameplay, the affinity sphere only tends to be the highest for so long, until it (and other spheres) hang at the Arete cap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T03:46:21-07:00","id":1341071,"title":"","content":"The idea, at least way back when, was that each Tradition's Sphere, especially the first dot of it, is innately tied to that Tradition's concept, paradigm and world view, and so every member of that Tradition learns that first dot as part of the initiation into the Tradition. For example, every Euthanatos has Entropy 1 because they have to be able to sense and recognize fate/fortune/destiny and causality in order to carry out the task of maintaining and protecting the Great Wheel, so that is the very first thing each of them is taught. The same with the other eight. An Akashic has to be aware of her own mind and how to center it, a Choruser has to be able to recognize the primal power of the One, an Ecstatic has to be able to feel the pulse of Lakashim, and so on. That is why every character got that first dot for free in addition to the five dots to spend however they wanted.<br /> <br /> (The Hermetics were a quasi-exception, largely owing to their Ars Magica origins. Forces was the Ars Essentia/Essential Art, and The Gateway to greater power and mastery, but because several Houses carried over from pre-Mage material, their focus sometimes rested on other spheres. But even then, the idea was that an apprentice would demonstrate their worth - step through The Gateway - by first showing an understanding of Ars Essentia and then moving on to the specifics of their House.)<br /> <br /> I have, for most of the past twenty years, had PCs start with both the Tradition Sphere and a Favored Sphere (one they are just naturally adept with or that they tend to focus on above all others), both with the same XP discounts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T05:26:52-07:00","id":1341080,"title":"","content":"So you get the experience discount on TWO spheres? The one you pick as affinity and the one your Faction offers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T07:38:52-07:00","id":1341088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341080#post1341080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you get the experience discount on TWO spheres? The one you pick as affinity and the one your Faction offers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Under my own personal house rules, yes. Under official M20, no. (Unless I missed something.)<br /> <br /> Under 1st, 2nd and Revised edition rules, everyone got their Tradition's Sphere and that was it, with IIRC Revised introducing the idea that certain factions within a Tradition might allow for an alternate Sphere (House Solificati, for example, having Matter rather than Forces). M20, which I admit to not being overly familiar with, apparently takes this even further by allowing you to pick from three different ones for each group<sup>1</sup>. But, just speaking from personal opinion, I'm not entirely wild about the idea because that first dot of each Tradition's specific Sphere is really the cornerstone of everything they do. But on the other side of the coin, I recognize that you will often have a character concept where what sort of magic they focus on will not match with the Tradition's Sphere. The Etherite biologist who focuses on Life, the Verbena weather witch mastering Forces, or the Celestial Choruser using Entropy to try and understand the One's grand plan and the divine fate of souls. Hence my house rule, which always seemed to work ok. <br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup>(My reading of the original text you quoted is that your single personal Affinity Sphere can be anything you want, but at least one of your Sphere dots has to be spent on one of the Spheres listed for your Tradition. The problem seems to be that &quot;affinity sphere&quot; is being used to describe two different things, the character's personal favored Sphere and the Spheres each Tradition specializes in. It should be using different terms for clarity.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T08:31:12-07:00","id":1341094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341088#post1341088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Under my own personal house rules, yes. Under official M20, no. (Unless I missed something.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I found something in the Book of Secrets, p.79.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dual Affiliation<br /> ...When raising a Sphere, your character gets to use the Affinity<br /> Sphere rate for one Sphere per group... </div> </div> </div>Implying that indeed you get the discount on your group AND the one you use as a mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341088#post1341088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(My reading of the original text you quoted is that your single personal Affinity Sphere can be anything you want, but at least one of your Sphere dots has to be spent on one of the Spheres listed for your Tradition. <b>The problem seems to be that &quot;affinity sphere&quot; is being used to describe two different things, the character's personal favored Sphere and the Spheres each Tradition specializes in. It should be using different terms for clarity.</b>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T15:32:10-07:00","id":1341157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341094#post1341094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Implying that indeed you get the discount on your group AND the one you use as a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. it just literally says that whatever you picked as your character's affinity sphere, from the list of the group they belong to, gets that cheaper rate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There is a Merit that lets you study under two groups - which is when you get two affinity spheres. Hence 'per group'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T18:45:48-07:00","id":1341192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341157#post1341157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. it just literally says that whatever you picked as your character's affinity sphere, from the list of the group they belong to, gets that cheaper rate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There is a Merit that lets you study under two groups - which is when you get two affinity spheres. Hence 'per group'.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, what I am saying is that<b> Dual Affiliation</b> is the merit that lets you study under 2 groups, and it says that &quot;<i>..When raising a Sphere, your character gets to use the Affinity Sphere rate for one Sphere per group... </i>&quot;<br /> <br /> So the Affinity Sphere discount goes per group (two groups with this merit), AND you get your regular Affinity Sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T20:51:09-07:00","id":1341209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341071#post1341071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(The Hermetics were a quasi-exception, largely owing to their Ars Magica origins. Forces was the Ars Essentia/Essential Art, and The Gateway to greater power and mastery, but because several Houses carried over from pre-Mage material, their focus sometimes rested on other spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ars Magica doesn't work that way at all. The only thing that really gets carried over is backstory, and even then there are major changes. As for mechanics, there is almost no similarity. There are no Spheres, and no direct equivalent to Forces. In the current version of that game, every magus gets a free Minor Virtue (+1 Merit) from their House. Tremere gets a focus in Certamen, Flambeau can choose Puissant Ignem or Puissant Perdo (or just about anything that fits their concept), Tytalus is Self Confident, Bjornaer is Heartbeast, and so on. My best guess, after reading OoH-Revised, is Brucato is a big time Ars fan and wanted to demonstrate that the OoH is not monolithic. In Mage, the easiest way to simulate diversity in magick is to have optional affinity Spheres.<br /> In Sorcerers Crusade, also written by Brucato, a Mage can pick any sphere as their Affinity Sphere. When I get around to running an M20 game someday, I am going to house-rule that option in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T22:48:53-07:00","id":1341222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341192#post1341192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Affinity Sphere discount goes per group (two groups with this merit), AND you get your regular Affinity Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under No One Of Consequence's hourserule, yes, as he does that extra non-faction mage-personal affinity sphere.<br /> Under normal rules, you only get an affinity sphere for each faction you belong to. Normaly one, with this merit two total.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T05:51:12-07:00","id":1341241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341222#post1341222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under No One Of Consequence's hourserule, yes, as he does that extra non-faction mage-personal affinity sphere.<br /> Under normal rules, you only get an affinity sphere for each faction you belong to. Normaly one, with this merit two total.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please correct me, but what I keep asking is clarity:<br /> <br /> <b>a.</b> You get an Affinity Sphere by being a mage (any sphere)<br /> <b>b. </b>You get one Affinity Sphere from your faction (does this affinity have to be one from point <b>a</b>?)<br /> <br /> Please correct me about points a and b. If a) and b) are different, you get two different Affinity Spheres. This seems be supported by the fact that the main book offers a single affinity by being a mage, and book of secrets talks about faction cost discount<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-14-2019, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T06:17:14-07:00","id":1341244,"title":"","content":"You get a single Affinity sphere.<br /> <br /> One.<br /> <br /> You get another one if you take a 7 point merit.<br /> <br /> &quot;Record Spheres (6, with the Affinity Sphere receiving the first dot).&quot; -From the Character creation quick guide.<br /> /THE/ Affinity sphere. Not Spheres.<br /> <br /> Also a few lines later<br /> <br /> &quot;The Affinity Sphere entry under each group gives the default Sphere for this sect. Some groups have more than one Sphere listed, but only one Affinity Sphere may be chosen per character. &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;All mages begin with one Affinity Sphere: &quot; Theres a bit after it that says 'you have to have one dot in your group's affinity sphere' but that quote is redundant, as you have to have an affinity sphere and it comes from your faction.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Affinity Sphere: Regardless of how you define what you do, there\u2019s one Sphere that inevitably means more to you than any other one: the affinity Sphere, your initial field of study and connection. This reflects your \u201cfirst kiss\u201d within the world of possibilities&quot; - One sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","user":"Jihelu","date":". 10-14-2019, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T07:06:03-07:00","id":1341247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341244#post1341244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get a single Affinity sphere.<br /> <br /> One.<br /> <br /> You get another one if you take a 7 point merit.<br /> <br /> &quot;Record Spheres (6, with the Affinity Sphere receiving the first dot).&quot; -From the Character creation quick guide.<br /> /THE/ Affinity sphere. Not Spheres.<br /> <br /> Also a few lines later<br /> <br /> &quot;The Affinity Sphere entry under each group gives the default Sphere for this sect. Some groups have more than one Sphere listed, but only one Affinity Sphere may be chosen per character. &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;All mages begin with one Affinity Sphere: &quot; There is a bit after it that says 'you have to have one dot in your group's affinity sphere' but that quote is redundant, as you have to have an affinity sphere and it comes from your faction.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Affinity Sphere: Regardless of how you define what you do, there\u2019s one Sphere that inevitably means more to you than any other one: the affinity Sphere, your initial field of study and connection. This reflects your \u201cfirst kiss\u201d within the world of possibilities&quot; - One sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks, this clarifies and also makes me angry, not the fact that there is a single Affinity Sphere, the fact that mechanically this is so confusing on one side; and that on the setting side, is RIDICULOUS that you have an affinity with certain magic and then only your <i>faction </i>can make you better at it...<br /> <br /> So if your affinity sphere comes from your faction there is no possible Syndicate Member with Affinity for Spirit, or Celestial Chorus member with Affinity for Entropy... Bonkers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Classic World of Darkness is so unnecessarily complex, inconsistent, and lacking crossover rules; that discourages play at some point. At least the Chronicles of Darkness have consistent mechanics for mortals and supernaturals (not similar power levels across gamelines, that is not the same thing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-14-2019, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T07:59:52-07:00","id":1341257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341247#post1341247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Classic World of Darkness is so unnecessarily complex, inconsistent, and lacking crossover rules; that discourages play at some point. At least the Chronicles of Darkness have consistent mechanics for mortals and supernaturals (not similar power levels across gamelines, that is not the same thing)</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally Classic is only confusing because of the 20th editions and the large amount of information for a unreliable narrator told Meta-plot. Lock of cross over and the confusing and contradictory meta-plot is why the world was destroyed in the first place and then the game lines were rebuilt with the 1st editions of Requiem and such. Those also had problems as they went the opposite way and tried to be sans-metaplot and this was not to the liking of many players as well as older players like myself liked the plot of classic and missed our favorite characters. Hince why chonicles has some plot and Classic is back with full on plot. However...<br /> <br /> The 20th anivarsary editions were supposed to be onmibuses and not truly an edition. So much context was left out of these &quot;editions&quot; that it greatly adds to the confusion. I am having a lot of trouble reading them and I have been witht he game since it first came out. they are just unweildy in their scope and leaves much to be desired. That being said there are some good gems in them with some of the rules changes but if you want it to make since you should really come into it from one of the older editions and since you can find good printings on e-bay cheap or run them from PDF I would suggest doing that. After playing with those editions I would then pick up 20th and do like I am doing now, muddle your way through.<br /> <br /> If none of that is to your liking I would recomend Awakening, especially the 2nd edition. I am a real fan of that edition, but I prefere my Ascension wars plotline enough to keep me coming back to Classic time and time again. There was a translation guide in Vampire from old to new and I don't know if they have one for Mage or not but that is another option to get the ascension war feel in Awakening. I have not read one though so i wouldn't know how good it is.<br /> <br /> Chronicles may be more up your ally especially since they are just now coming out with contageon chronicles which is a crossover chronicle for the CoD line. I hear good things but have not got to play it yet.<br /> <br /> All in all no need to fret, there are so many different ways to play the game that you can find one that fits your style and joy for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T08:36:26-07:00","id":1341263,"title":"","content":"If you want to be a NWO/Syndicate member that specializes completely in Spirit (IE: Affinity sphere) just take dual traditions.<br /> <br /> Or just take spirit as another sphere and recognize it just takes a bit more effort to be good at it. The affinity sphere is like, a small exp bonus. You don't immense unlimited power from it. It also has no bearing on any other sphere you take.<br /> <br /> Edit: Nothing says only your faction can make you better at it. Self study, talking to other factions that also specialize in it a bit (Most traditions/Technocracy groups have like, 2-3 affinity spheres after all. Also all of the Technocracy can cross train every sphere without penalties). <br /> There are rules/a paragraph or two talking about possible penalties of learning with someone who you don't 100% agree with metaphysically.<br /> <br /> Go learn Mind from an Akashic Master, go learn Life from a Verbena, go be broad as fuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","user":"Jihelu","date":". 10-14-2019, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T08:39:14-07:00","id":1341264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341263#post1341263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The affinity sphere is like, a small exp bonus. You don't immense unlimited power from it. It also has no bearing on any other sphere you take.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Aside of the small XP bonus, the affinity sphere has no special effects. And as I said, it is not even a rule that it has to be the highest sphere - just the average norm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T17:51:04-07:00","id":1341355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341041-affinity-sphere-confusion?p=1341264#post1341264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. Aside of the small XP bonus, the affinity sphere has no special effects. And as I said, it is not even a rule that it has to be the highest sphere - just the average norm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You are right, it is more the lack of coherence and clarity... Sorry to rant, for my this is the last of a list of minutiae that is annoying, both on the fluff and mechanical side.<br /> <br /> I love the setting, I love the metaplot, the rich history, but I hate the clumsy mechanics interactions between different supers, the lack of clear rules for certain interactions... I was told that I have to understand the original game setting, the young game designers at the time, the excessive &quot;granola-thinking&quot; on some old lore... And that some new developers have to work on top of that to keep the feeling of the original setting.<br /> <br /> Well, at least now I understand Affinity rules. Thanks to all who helped clarify the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-14-2019, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}